12:["$","$L11","016",{"a":{"id":"016","slug":"account-persona","term":"Account Persona","category":"creative","kind":"essay","image":"account-persona","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["hook-slop","creative-matrix","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","dek":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return..","point":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.","body":["Write the opinions this account can defend and the topics it leaves to others. A rushed student does not discuss an app like an organizational consultant. Character appears through chosen details, not a biography full of adjectives. A fictional persona should be identifiable as such when it could be mistaken for a real person.","Test the character against a frustration. What happens when the app does not solve everything? A credible voice can acknowledge a limit, propose a manual workaround or reject an unsuitable use. If the persona only praises the product, its identity may collapse when the audience asks an unexpected question. A consistent boundary often reveals more character than another carefully chosen visual accessory."],"action":["Write three opinions and three refusals.","Test consistency across five scripts."],"trap":"An invented testimonial does not become acceptable because a persona delivers it.","quote":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A persona is not a photo and a name.","text":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return..","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Account Persona","text":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An invented testimonial does not become acceptable because a persona delivers it.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write three opinions and three refusals.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Test consistency across five scripts.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/account-persona.jpg","width":1280,"height":875,"alt":{"en":"Carved stone theatrical masks displayed among the ruins of Ostia Antica."},"credit":"Dennis G. Jarvis","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 5a244f48cf59ebe7c71fe44087df41410beb2633.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italy_-_Ostia_Antica_-_Theatre_Masks_(5149585364).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
13:["$","$L11","017",{"a":{"id":"017","slug":"hook-slop","term":"Hook Slop","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"hook-slop","tier":"editorial","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["faceless-account","account-persona","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","dek":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value.","point":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value. It is an editorial criticism, not a platform category.","body":["A good opening makes a promise the rest fulfills. “I lost my notes before the exam” creates a specific situation. “This app will change your life” could sell anything. Compare the first sentence with the conclusion: if they address different problems, early retention may measure delayed disappointment.","Try rewriting without commands or spectacular adjectives. Replace the demand to stay with the situation you will resolve. If the opening becomes clearer, precision has improved. Then evaluate the full piece: a quieter hook may attract fewer curious viewers and more people facing the actual problem. That possibility is worth testing, not asserting as a universal advantage of restrained creative work."],"action":["Connect the opening to visible evidence.","Remove superlatives that add nothing."],"trap":"Better opening retention does not guarantee that the promise is delivered later.","quote":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"“Stop scrolling”: everybody is shouting the same thing.","text":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Hook Slop","text":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value. It is an editorial criticism, not a platform category.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Better opening retention does not guarantee that the promise is delivered later.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Connect the opening to visible evidence.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Remove superlatives that add nothing.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/hook-slop.jpg","width":1280,"height":1707,"alt":{"en":"A red and cream handheld megaphone with a coiled microphone cord."},"credit":"Solomon203","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 20e7e1574fe6745909375e5658e0229e84fcafe0.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seikaku_ER-56_20190217.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
14:["$","$L11","018",{"a":{"id":"018","slug":"faceless-account","term":"Faceless Account","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"faceless-account","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["formatted-account","hook-slop","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Faceless. Not voiceless.","dek":"A Faceless Account creates content without relying on its operator’s visible face.","point":"A Faceless Account creates content without relying on its operator’s visible face. Topic, narration and visual choices can still make it recognizable.","body":["An annotated screen recording can express a stronger opinion than a talking avatar. For an app, show a use and its constraints: a failed search, a useful setting, a decision. Viewers should leave with something even if they never see your face. Check rights to any footage used.","For a demo, use your own recording with clearly labeled fictional data. Focus on the useful action and remove personal information. Narration can address a common mistake or a difficult decision. This gives the content personality without needing a face, an invented customer or an imitation of a known creator. The audience still receives a concrete explanation it can assess independently."],"action":["Define a consistent visual language.","Record a complete, understandable action."],"trap":"An absent face does not erase transparency requirements or other creators’ rights.","quote":"Faceless. Not voiceless.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Faceless. Not voiceless.","text":"A Faceless Account creates content without relying on its operator’s visible face.","media":"/images/editorial/faceless-account.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Faceless Account","text":"A Faceless Account creates content without relying on its operator’s visible face. Topic, narration and visual choices can still make it recognizable.","media":"/images/editorial/faceless-account.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An absent face does not erase transparency requirements or other creators’ rights.","media":"/images/editorial/faceless-account.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define a consistent visual language.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/faceless-account.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Record a complete, understandable action.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/faceless-account.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/faceless-account.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"A motorcyclist appears as a dark silhouette between headlights on a street at night."},"credit":"Tiomax80","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 28b410648b8d738726989e99d05ce42fe2b6b720.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Night_silhouettes._(9722264213).jpg","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
15:["$","$L11","019",{"a":{"id":"019","slug":"formatted-account","term":"Formatted Account","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"formatted-account","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["chaotic-account","faceless-account","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A recurring format beats an empty template.","dek":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize.","point":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize. Repetition concerns the promise, not necessarily the substance.","body":["“One setting, one avoided mistake” is a format: every episode can teach something different. A colored background with three arbitrary sentences is only a template. Record what stays fixed and what varies. That separation makes testing clearer while preventing the series from exhausting itself.","A useful episode may slightly break its format to serve the subject. Keep the promise but adjust length when the explanation requires it. Record that exception so it is not confused with a strategic change. Consistency helps readers recognize what they receive; it should not become a restriction that prevents explanation. A format earns its place by making good ideas easier to deliver."],"action":["Define the recurring promise in one sentence.","Prepare ten episodes with different lessons."],"trap":"Recognizing a format does not guarantee the next episode offers anything new.","quote":"A recurring format beats an empty template.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A recurring format beats an empty template.","text":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-account.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Formatted Account","text":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize. Repetition concerns the promise, not necessarily the substance.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-account.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Recognizing a format does not guarantee the next episode offers anything new.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-account.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define the recurring promise in one sentence.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-account.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Prepare ten episodes with different lessons.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-account.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/formatted-account.jpg","width":1280,"height":960,"alt":{"en":"Repeating rounded concrete balconies on Chicago’s River City apartments."},"credit":"w_lemay","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 23b78937a31d7f80187e6a7a408758763669adfd.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River_City,_Wells_Street_and_Polk_Street,_Chicago,_IL_-_54519335782.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
16:["$","$L11","020",{"a":{"id":"020","slug":"chaotic-account","term":"Chaotic Account","category":"creative","kind":"essay","image":"chaotic-account","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["ai-persona","formatted-account","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A chaotic account still has a point of view.","dek":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template.","point":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template. In AGD, chaotic means flexible, not devoid of audience or logic.","body":["A founder can post a screenshot, an anecdote and a demo without losing their voice. The connection is their view of work. Organize content by purpose: explain, entertain, expose friction. Otherwise the week’s strongest post becomes an excuse to chase every trend.","Imagine a week built around missed appointments: a meme, an anecdote and a practical demonstration. Formats change while the problem remains recognizable. Compare responses within that content family. You can learn which treatment clarifies the situation without reducing the entire editorial direction to the format producing the biggest spike. This preserves flexibility while providing a meaningful basis for the next creative decision."],"action":["Keep a common audience across formats.","Label each post by purpose."],"trap":"Format diversity can complicate attribution; document what actually changed.","quote":"A chaotic account still has a point of view.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A chaotic account still has a point of view.","text":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template.","media":"/images/editorial/chaotic-account.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Chaotic Account","text":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template. In AGD, chaotic means flexible, not devoid of audience or logic.","media":"/images/editorial/chaotic-account.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Format diversity can complicate attribution; document what actually changed.","media":"/images/editorial/chaotic-account.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Keep a common audience across formats.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/chaotic-account.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Label each post by purpose.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/chaotic-account.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/chaotic-account.jpg","width":1280,"height":960,"alt":{"en":"Graffiti, wall paintings, and parked bicycles on an Amsterdam street."},"credit":"Fons Heijnsbroek","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: d99302b5d7a919d63639110e4b3951ed8c4c5f9f.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wall-paintings_and_urban_art_on_the_walls_in_Amsterdam_city.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
17:["$","$L11","021",{"a":{"id":"021","slug":"ai-persona","term":"AI Persona","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"ai-persona","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["persona-agd","chaotic-account","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A synthetic character needs something to say.","dek":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production.","point":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production. Its editorial value still depends on coherence and usefulness.","body":["Define continuity: what the character knows, does not know, likes and never claims to have experienced. A fictional narrator can tell an illustrative story, not provide a fake customer testimonial. Inconsistent voice or recurring details break identity faster than imperfect rendering. Keep a reference sheet and identify the fiction.","A continuity sheet can include preferred vocabulary, editorial positions and consistent visual details. Add subjects where the character does not offer expert judgment. Stability supports production while transparency supports reader understanding. The aim is coherent fiction, not an imaginary person presented as an actual customer. Review both image and script because a careful disclosure cannot repair contradictory claims inside the content itself."],"action":["Write the character’s boundaries.","Review scripts for invented real-world experiences."],"trap":"A realistic appearance is not evidence of expertise or product use.","quote":"A synthetic character needs something to say.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A synthetic character needs something to say.","text":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production.","media":"/images/editorial/ai-persona.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"AI Persona","text":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production. Its editorial value still depends on coherence and usefulness.","media":"/images/editorial/ai-persona.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A realistic appearance is not evidence of expertise or product use.","media":"/images/editorial/ai-persona.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write the character’s boundaries.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/ai-persona.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Review scripts for invented real-world experiences.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/ai-persona.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/ai-persona.jpg","width":1280,"height":1214,"alt":{"en":"A seated fashion mannequin dressed in dark clothes in a Paris shop window."},"credit":"Ввласенко","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 124997d1f6190a84a1df6987fe9a4899cae645d4.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mannequin_in_the_shop_window._Paris,_France.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
18:["$","$L11","022",{"a":{"id":"022","slug":"persona-agd","term":"Persona AGD","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"persona-agd","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["slideshow-agd","ai-persona","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"One product. Three narrators. Three reasons.","dek":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts..","point":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts.","body":["For a calendar tool, consider clearly fictional perspectives: a juggling freelancer, a revising student, a coordinating parent. Each encounters a specific problem. The difference must appear in the scenario, not merely a displayed age. Then examine whether audiences and their questions actually differ.","Build a scenario grid and look for duplicates. If all three narrators always encounter the same situation in the same words, their biographies are doing no work. Rewrite from each character’s constraints. A credible difference in context is more useful than a catalog of psychological traits invented to fill a brief. Evaluate the published content against those constraints rather than the personas’ decorative descriptions."],"action":["Connect each persona to a specific friction.","Avoid having them repeat the same sales script."],"trap":"Three characters do not prove you reached three different audiences.","quote":"One product. Three narrators. Three reasons.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"One product. Three narrators. Three reasons.","text":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts..","media":"/images/editorial/persona-agd.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Persona AGD","text":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts.","media":"/images/editorial/persona-agd.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Three characters do not prove you reached three different audiences.","media":"/images/editorial/persona-agd.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Connect each persona to a specific friction.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/persona-agd.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Avoid having them repeat the same sales script.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/persona-agd.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/persona-agd.jpg","width":1280,"height":960,"alt":{"en":"An empty ornate theatre with golden balconies, a decorated ceiling, and rows of seats."},"credit":"Avacado-pie","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 6b5398d1da234f7ae8a607929282ac89a233cf97.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paramount_Theatre_Seating_View_(empty).jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
19:["$","$L11","023",{"a":{"id":"023","slug":"slideshow-agd","term":"Slideshow AGD","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"slideshow-agd","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["story-slideshow","persona-agd","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A slideshow is a story, not a sliced PDF.","dek":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows.","point":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows. A useful sequence progresses, giving a clear reason to reach the next screen.","body":["Write the transitions first: situation, complication, discovery, application. A slide can hold one idea without becoming empty. If every screen repeats the first screen’s promise, readers move without learning. Read the sequence without design to check progression before polishing typography.","An educational sequence can start with a poor result, show its cause and offer a correction. Images should help viewers see the difference rather than merely occupy space. Check text size, contrast and visual load on every slide. A mobile slideshow should remain readable without constant zooming. Its narrative structure and physical legibility work together; neither compensates for the absence of the other."],"action":["Give each slide a purpose.","Keep a conclusion useful without another click."],"trap":"More slides do not mean more value or better distribution.","quote":"A slideshow is a story, not a sliced PDF.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A slideshow is a story, not a sliced PDF.","text":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-agd.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Slideshow AGD","text":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows. A useful sequence progresses, giving a clear reason to reach the next screen.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-agd.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"More slides do not mean more value or better distribution.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-agd.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Give each slide a purpose.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-agd.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep a conclusion useful without another click.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-agd.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/slideshow-agd.jpg","width":1280,"height":1019,"alt":{"en":"A vintage slide projector with its large lens and upright slide holder."},"credit":"Berthold Werner","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 27154a4bcea6fba329e9b96074e7df16ef08581f.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Super_Zett_III_Slide_projektor_BW_2025-07-25_16-38-31_stack.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1a:["$","$L11","024",{"a":{"id":"024","slug":"story-slideshow","term":"Story Slideshow","category":"creative","kind":"essay","image":"story-slideshow","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["educational-slideshow","slideshow-agd","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A little tension beats fifteen advice slides.","dek":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution.","point":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution. Its value is narrative; it does not depend on a magic slide count.","body":["Open with a concrete choice: recover your notes or improvise in front of a client. Show what complicates the choice and what resolves it. A product can enter when it becomes useful. Remove it from the draft: if the entire scene collapses, you may have written an ad without a story.","Write two endings before production: one shows what the person learned, another immediately pushes a purchase. If the first better serves the subject, keep it. A CTA can follow without stealing the resolution. Readers should distinguish the story’s value from the commercial next step. This also makes it possible to test that next step without rebuilding the entire narrative each time."],"action":["Write the conflict in one line.","Show the resolution instead of announcing it."],"trap":"Do not invent a customer outcome to make the ending more convincing.","quote":"A little tension beats fifteen advice slides.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A little tension beats fifteen advice slides.","text":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution.","media":"/images/editorial/story-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Story Slideshow","text":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution. Its value is narrative; it does not depend on a magic slide count.","media":"/images/editorial/story-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Do not invent a customer outcome to make the ending more convincing.","media":"/images/editorial/story-slideshow.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write the conflict in one line.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/story-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Show the resolution instead of announcing it.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/story-slideshow.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/story-slideshow.jpg","width":1280,"height":851,"alt":{"en":"An analogue cinema projector displayed outside the Onomichi Cinema Museum."},"credit":"Asturio Cantabrio","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: ec961929acd5111ad04a302fe37a8e9bc5f6215a.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Onomichi_Cinema_Museum_film_projector_ac_(1).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1b:["$","$L11","025",{"a":{"id":"025","slug":"educational-slideshow","term":"Educational Slideshow","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"educational-slideshow","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["meme-slideshow","story-slideshow","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Teach something before the final slide.","dek":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading.","point":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading. Its entire promise should not be deferred to a sales page.","body":["Take a narrow question: how do median and mean differ? A small, explicitly illustrative numerical example is enough. Show the calculation and the decision it changes. The last screen can suggest further reading, but earlier screens should already answer the original question.","To explain a misleading average, show a few fictional values and place the large outcome beside them. Readers can repeat the calculation and see why the conclusion changes. This verifiability makes the sequence stronger than an impressive number standing alone. It also creates a useful transition to a longer note for readers wanting more detail, while leaving the original slideshow complete on its own."],"action":["Choose an answerable question.","Include an example and a limitation."],"trap":"A definition without application often leaves all useful work to the reader.","quote":"Teach something before the final slide.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Teach something before the final slide.","text":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading.","media":"/images/editorial/educational-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Educational Slideshow","text":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading. Its entire promise should not be deferred to a sales page.","media":"/images/editorial/educational-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A definition without application often leaves all useful work to the reader.","media":"/images/editorial/educational-slideshow.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Choose an answerable question.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/educational-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Include an example and a limitation.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/educational-slideshow.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/educational-slideshow.jpg","width":1280,"height":811,"alt":{"en":"The concrete exterior and geometric forms of Brunel University’s lecture theatre building."},"credit":"Suntooooth","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 1349fdb7d3f3dc2e0871b89c07f79bb928de3bef.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brunel_University_lecture_theatre_2024-04-12_(cropped).png","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1c:["$","$L11","026",{"a":{"id":"026","slug":"meme-slideshow","term":"Meme Slideshow","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"meme-slideshow","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["product-discovery","educational-slideshow","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The joke should work without the logo.","dek":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline.","point":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline. A product can fit inside it, but cannot replace the comic mechanism.","body":["Useful material often comes from a friction your audience instantly recognizes. Three meetings to decide to cancel one, for example. Show the text to someone in the intended audience. Ask what they recognized, not whether they liked it. Qualitative feedback helps separate resonance from politeness.","The punchline can target a habit rather than a person. A recognizable shared behavior provides material without inventing customer quotes. Keep a fictional situation’s status clear. Comic precision often comes from one convincing detail rather than a spectacular claim about how many people experience the scene. That leaves space for humor while preserving the distinction between an observation, an illustration and actual research."],"action":["Start with a specific observation.","Check rights to reused images."],"trap":"A successful joke does not automatically validate product positioning.","quote":"The joke should work without the logo.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The joke should work without the logo.","text":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline.","media":"/images/editorial/meme-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Meme Slideshow","text":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline. A product can fit inside it, but cannot replace the comic mechanism.","media":"/images/editorial/meme-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A successful joke does not automatically validate product positioning.","media":"/images/editorial/meme-slideshow.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Start with a specific observation.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/meme-slideshow.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Check rights to reused images.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/meme-slideshow.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/meme-slideshow.jpg","width":1280,"height":960,"alt":{"en":"A playful illustrated street mural displayed on an outdoor construction fence in Łódź."},"credit":"Mariochom","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 8f2ee9c6d97afce8e29553b1f6663617a8c3e771.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%81%C3%B3d%C5%BA-canvas_with_funny_graphics.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1d:["$","$L11","027",{"a":{"id":"027","slug":"product-discovery","term":"Product Discovery","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"product-discovery","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["brainrotization","meme-slideshow","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The product enters when it becomes useful.","dek":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case.","point":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case. An editorial approach does not remove the need to disclose a relevant commercial relationship.","body":["Show the task before the interface. For a video tool, the subject might be adapting an edit to three formats. Explain what stays manual, what gets easier and where results fail. A demo retaining limitations helps readers more than a context-free feature list.","A complementary tool can appear when the workflow needs it. Google Sheets, for example, can organize ideas before production. Explain its exact role and what information moves to the next step. A logo list explains little; a clearly described transition lets readers repeat the work using their own setup. This gives adjacent products a reason to appear beyond lending credibility to a promotional collection."],"action":["Describe the job to be done.","Show a real limitation of the solution."],"trap":"A subtle mention should not conceal who benefits commercially from the content.","quote":"The product enters when it becomes useful.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The product enters when it becomes useful.","text":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case.","media":"/images/editorial/product-discovery.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Product Discovery","text":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case. An editorial approach does not remove the need to disclose a relevant commercial relationship.","media":"/images/editorial/product-discovery.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A subtle mention should not conceal who benefits commercially from the content.","media":"/images/editorial/product-discovery.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Describe the job to be done.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/product-discovery.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Show a real limitation of the solution.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/product-discovery.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/product-discovery.jpg","width":1280,"height":848,"alt":{"en":"A wood and metal bookcase with shelves, drawers, plants, and records in a workshop interior."},"credit":"Micheli Design","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: abae288e07415059ba5ed386b74934ebeedf1341.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Custom-made_industrial_wood_and_metal_bookcase_%E2%80%93_Micheli_Design.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
1e:["$","$L11","028",{"a":{"id":"028","slug":"brainrotization","term":"Brainrotization","category":"creative","kind":"essay","image":"brainrotization","tier":"editorial","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["creative-brief","product-discovery","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Marketing caught brainrot. What next?","dek":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats.","point":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats. It describes neither a medical condition nor a cognitive measurement.","body":["Absurdity can create a shared language, but it can also erase the subject. Ask what remains after the joke: an idea, a recognized problem, a useful memory? Frenetic editing need not be condemned by default. It should pass the same coherence test as the quietest video.","Absurd content can still identify its status: sketch, metaphor or invented example. That framing prevents a joke from becoming commercial evidence in an out-of-context screenshot. Work on the punchline and legibility together. Audiences can enjoy chaotic form without wanting to decode an incomprehensible demonstration. The useful question is whether the chosen absurdity sharpens the point or merely delays its arrival."],"action":["Summarize the message without describing effects.","Test understanding with the intended audience."],"trap":"Provocative cultural language does not justify claims about audience health or attention.","quote":"Marketing caught brainrot. What next?","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Marketing caught brainrot. What next?","text":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats.","media":"/images/editorial/brainrotization.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Brainrotization","text":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats. It describes neither a medical condition nor a cognitive measurement.","media":"/images/editorial/brainrotization.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Provocative cultural language does not justify claims about audience health or attention.","media":"/images/editorial/brainrotization.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Summarize the message without describing effects.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/brainrotization.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Test understanding with the intended audience.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/brainrotization.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/brainrotization.jpg","width":1280,"height":850,"alt":{"en":"A row of illuminated arcade cabinets in a games exhibition."},"credit":"Staffan Vilcans","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: a43ae782ce93d9fa18b56b39cb11d8b819098d53.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arcade_machines_-_13332978733.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1f:["$","$L11","029",{"a":{"id":"029","slug":"creative-brief","term":"Creative Brief","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"creative-brief","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["hook-payoff","brainrotization","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A good brief starts with what we want to learn.","dek":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis.","point":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis. It gives a creator direction and an analyst an interpretable question.","body":["Replace “make a viral video” with “test whether this friction resonates with students revising.” List requirements, freedoms and boundaries. A useful constraint explains its role: the first screen should make the situation visible, not merely contain a keyword.","Add the sentence a viewer should be able to repeat afterward. It is not a mandatory slogan but a comprehension check. If the creative team proposes a better way to convey the idea, the brief should allow it. The document sets the job’s objective without confusing that objective with the first imagined solution. This distinction keeps constraints useful while preserving the creator’s judgment."],"action":["Write the learning question.","Define what the creator can choose freely."],"trap":"An overly prescriptive brief can eliminate the variation the test was meant to explore.","quote":"A good brief starts with what we want to learn.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A good brief starts with what we want to learn.","text":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-brief.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Creative Brief","text":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis. It gives a creator direction and an analyst an interpretable question.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-brief.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An overly prescriptive brief can eliminate the variation the test was meant to explore.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-brief.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write the learning question.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-brief.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Define what the creator can choose freely.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-brief.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/creative-brief.jpg","width":1280,"height":924,"alt":{"en":"An archival photograph of printers working at benches in the Deli Courant typesetting workshop."},"credit":"Rijksmuseum","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: bdc598ccc83875350e8488c22995634e31cdafff.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zetterij_van_de_Deli_Courant,_NG-1990-14-39.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
20:["$","$L11","030",{"a":{"id":"030","slug":"hook-payoff","term":"Hook & payoff","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"hook-payoff","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["creative-library","creative-brief","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The hook’s promise must be paid back.","dek":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise.","point":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise. Its alignment with the hook is checked in the content, not only in a retention curve.","body":["If the opening promises an expensive mistake, show the mistake and how to avoid it. A vague revelation in the final second does not repay the promise. Read the sequence as a contract: what did the viewer agree to by staying? This check may remove a strong but misleading opening.","A simple audit shows only the beginning and asks what a person expects. Then reveal the ending. The gap between expectation and answer helps expose unintended promises. This feedback is not a representative measurement of your market, but it can uncover incoherence before full production. Keep the observed confusion in the brief so the next revision addresses a concrete problem rather than somebody’s vague preference."],"action":["Write promise and resolution side by side.","Check that the resolution is clearly shown."],"trap":"Keeping an audience through confusion is not the same as delivering value.","quote":"The hook’s promise must be paid back.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The hook’s promise must be paid back.","text":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-payoff.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Hook & payoff","text":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise. Its alignment with the hook is checked in the content, not only in a retention curve.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-payoff.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Keeping an audience through confusion is not the same as delivering value.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-payoff.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write promise and resolution side by side.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-payoff.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Check that the resolution is clearly shown.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/hook-payoff.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/hook-payoff.jpg","width":1280,"height":1623,"alt":{"en":"A fishing figure silhouetted atop a lighthouse beneath a warm orange sunset."},"credit":"Petar Milošević","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: e99fef0dea0e1c8e1ae36c1a45caa61d9cde8705.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fishing_by_lighthouse_at_sunset_(Adriatic_Sea).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
21:["$","$L11","031",{"a":{"id":"031","slug":"creative-library","term":"Creative Library","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"creative-library","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["format-fatigue","hook-payoff","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Your creative library is not a final_final folder.","dek":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results.","point":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results. It lets a team recover an idea and its test conditions without relying on memory.","body":["Give the concept an identifier, then identify its versions. Keep the brief, image sources, intended markets and associated posts. A filename cannot explain what changed. A winning version without context quickly becomes a template copied for the wrong reasons.","Add a short note after every test: what was published, how versions differed and the limits of interpretation. Avoid renaming every strong file “winner.” Content can win on views and lose on product understanding. Precise annotations make an archive usable by a new colleague or agent without requiring them to reconstruct the campaign from scattered messages and the memory of its original owner."],"action":["Connect each asset to its concept.","Keep licenses and published versions."],"trap":"An asset in a shared drive is not automatically licensed for every account or market.","quote":"Your creative library is not a final_final folder.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Your creative library is not a final_final folder.","text":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-library.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Creative Library","text":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results. It lets a team recover an idea and its test conditions without relying on memory.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-library.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An asset in a shared drive is not automatically licensed for every account or market.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-library.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Connect each asset to its concept.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-library.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep licenses and published versions.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-library.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/creative-library.jpg","width":1280,"height":736,"alt":{"en":"A narrow library aisle with bookshelves and a window looking out onto green trees."},"credit":"Scntst0009","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 8aa0653c477e3a0a8a6be354856fd77dde899b34.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Library_shelves_iitd.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
22:["$","$L11","032",{"a":{"id":"032","slug":"format-fatigue","term":"Format fatigue","category":"creative","kind":"essay","image":"format-fatigue","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["creative-matrix","creative-library","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The format works. Until it just repeats.","dek":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition.","point":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition. Studying it requires separating repetition from weaker topics and audience changes.","body":["Do not abandon a series after two weak episodes. Compare topics, promises and observation maturity. Test a structural variation addressing the same problem. If every format declines together, looking only for a creative explanation may hide another cause.","Separate new viewers from returning audiences when data allows. A format can feel repetitive to the team while remaining new to much of the audience. The reverse can also happen: creators still enjoy a series while responses suggest fatigue. Ground the decision in observable context rather than internal enthusiasm alone. Where those audience distinctions cannot be measured, state the uncertainty instead of filling it with assumptions."],"action":["Compare episodes at equal observation ages.","Test a variation before abandoning the series."],"trap":"A decline does not prove audience fatigue; the cause may remain unknown.","quote":"The format works. Until it just repeats.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The format works. Until it just repeats.","text":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition.","media":"/images/editorial/format-fatigue.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Format fatigue","text":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition. Studying it requires separating repetition from weaker topics and audience changes.","media":"/images/editorial/format-fatigue.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A decline does not prove audience fatigue; the cause may remain unknown.","media":"/images/editorial/format-fatigue.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Compare episodes at equal observation ages.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/format-fatigue.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Test a variation before abandoning the series.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/format-fatigue.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/format-fatigue.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"A macro photograph of the concentric grooves on a vinyl record."},"credit":"Evan-Amos","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 13066ddb840fd0edc705d1355a26db24f3285fc1.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:12in-LP-Vinyl-Record-Macro-Grooves.jpg","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/"}},"lang":"en"}]
23:["$","$L11","033",{"a":{"id":"033","slug":"creative-matrix","term":"Creative Matrix","category":"creative","kind":"guide","image":"creative-matrix","tier":"operating","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["account-persona","format-fatigue","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The matrix that stops fifty copies from being born.","dek":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format.","point":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format. It helps select experiments rather than mechanically filling every cell.","body":["Start with a few credible combinations. One problem may deserve a demo and a narrative without needing a meme. Record why each combination could work. Empty cells are useful: sometimes they reveal a missing idea rather than insufficient output.","An interesting cell should become a brief. Write the opening situation, the difference offered and the question to measure. If none of those sentences comes easily, leave the cell empty. The matrix is a selection tool: its value may be reducing productions that do not yet have a subject. A small set of explainable experiments is easier to learn from than an exhaustive but arbitrary catalog."],"action":["Cross three audiences with three relevant angles.","Reject combinations without an editorial reason."],"trap":"A full table is not proof of diversity if every scenario says the same thing.","quote":"The matrix that stops fifty copies from being born.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The matrix that stops fifty copies from being born.","text":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-matrix.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Creative Matrix","text":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format. It helps select experiments rather than mechanically filling every cell.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-matrix.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A full table is not proof of diversity if every scenario says the same thing.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-matrix.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Cross three audiences with three relevant angles.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-matrix.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Reject combinations without an editorial reason.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-matrix.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/creative-matrix.jpg","width":1280,"height":720,"alt":{"en":"Colorful Amsterdam canal houses and illuminated windows reflected in the water at blue hour."},"credit":"Basile Morin","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 552058bafe635df809ac18513f7f7490715e5706.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colorful_windows_and_canal_houses_at_blue_hour_with_water_reflection_in_Damrak_Amsterdam_Netherlands.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
